{"seq":32,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.683Z","runId":"failure-no-rework","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-1 Enforce expiry when resolving, and keep the row: Store the expiry on the link and compare it with the current time in LinkService.resolve. Expired rows are not deleted.","rationale":"The owner must still read the stats of an expired link, and the visitor must be told it expired rather than that it never existed. Both need the row to remain. The check reuses the row the redirect already loads.","alternatives":["A background job that deletes expired links: loses the statistics and turns expiry into a 404","Filter expired rows in the SQL WHERE clause: cannot tell expired from unknown, so it cannot answer 410"],"basedOn":"e33074890575c672324d968694418efee44551b9cea1beee1f12aeeca37275ed"},"prevHash":"1f13bf3a655889c99d3cf441af5cd2f832a7adf293af81c0991a2ed90ba52426","hash":"e3115e3f28c8c6f1f01204aa671fe79da42ae65a68802b3723e8148c26eb10d1"}
{"seq":33,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.683Z","runId":"failure-no-rework","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-2 410 Gone with a link_expired code: An expired link's redirect answers 410 as a problem document with code link_expired, and sends no Location header.","rationale":"410 is the HTTP status for a resource that existed and is intentionally gone, and it keeps the response in the API's existing error format.","alternatives":["404: indistinguishable from a mistyped link","An HTML explanation page: a new presentation concern for an API service"],"basedOn":"e33074890575c672324d968694418efee44551b9cea1beee1f12aeeca37275ed"},"prevHash":"e3115e3f28c8c6f1f01204aa671fe79da42ae65a68802b3723e8148c26eb10d1","hash":"c45ce411aaacf9646baec7d2bd2954aca356863b282340f30b777a93d3e553f4"}
{"seq":34,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.683Z","runId":"failure-no-rework","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-3 Two input forms, one stored form: Accept expiresAt or ttlSeconds but not both, require a time zone on expiresAt, require the result to be in the future, cap ttlSeconds at five years, and store a UTC instant.","rationale":"Campaigns end at a known time; temporary links are easier to express as a duration. Normalizing to one UTC value means the rest of the system handles a single representation. Requiring a zone avoids guessing which local time the caller meant.","alternatives":["Only expiresAt: forces clients to compute a timestamp for simple cases","Accept local times without a zone: ambiguous"],"basedOn":"e33074890575c672324d968694418efee44551b9cea1beee1f12aeeca37275ed"},"prevHash":"c45ce411aaacf9646baec7d2bd2954aca356863b282340f30b777a93d3e553f4","hash":"4cc2982ccb6cae579918992aee887096773268cbfa180cec2eeabeefc75329d1"}
{"seq":35,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.683Z","runId":"failure-no-rework","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-4 An expired alias stays reserved: Creating a link with the alias of an expired link returns 409 as before.","rationale":"Reuse would let anyone take over a link that is already printed, shared or bookmarked.","alternatives":["Release the alias on expiry: convenient for owners, unsafe for visitors"],"basedOn":"e33074890575c672324d968694418efee44551b9cea1beee1f12aeeca37275ed"},"prevHash":"4cc2982ccb6cae579918992aee887096773268cbfa180cec2eeabeefc75329d1","hash":"26bdc92233b2dc5107742d5ee49de19cb1e4e43437c6ddd15a05f9966094e680"}
{"seq":36,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.683Z","runId":"failure-no-rework","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-5 Fix BUG-17 by flushing in the close hook: ClickRecorder.close stops the timer and flushes. The onClose hook calls it inside a try/catch that logs how many events were lost if the flush fails.","rationale":"It removes the loss for every graceful shutdown, which is what a deployment is, without touching the redirect path. A failing final flush must not turn a shutdown into a hang.","alternatives":["Write each click synchronously in the redirect: also survives a crash, but breaks the requirement that recording never slows a redirect","Shorten the flush interval: narrows the window, does not close it"],"basedOn":"e33074890575c672324d968694418efee44551b9cea1beee1f12aeeca37275ed"},"prevHash":"26bdc92233b2dc5107742d5ee49de19cb1e4e43437c6ddd15a05f9966094e680","hash":"5e77d6a393e51d427fdc9075299f47faf4c543a8251b981d2b73f989ff35c82f"}
